{
  "additional_concerns": [
    "The encoded constant true answers activation only under the stipulated independent-footnote reading. It does not establish performance, compliance with paragraphs 10–13, or smart-contract integrity. TRUE_IS_SATISFIED must not override the typed DUTY_TRIGGER meaning.",
    "Footnote 5 can instead be read as specifying the minimum content of paragraph 14's request-conditioned demonstration. Its omission of the request phrase does not conclusively establish an independent trigger. Preserve both readings pending reconciliation.",
    "The substantive-responsibility candidate has no executable meaning. The supplied passages do not establish a complete authority, supervision and outcomes test, an assessment period, or severity and remediation thresholds. Actual facts and the applicable standard remain necessary.",
    "Section 6.11C concerns outsourced valuation. Its supervision standard cannot automatically be transferred to every tokenisation arrangement. Section 6.8's request concerns the register's address, not activation of footnote 5 demonstration.",
    "Proper ownership records and operational compatibility are expressly required, but neither alone establishes complete discharge of retained responsibility. Footnote 2 and the complete paragraphs 10–13 are not supplied; intermediary paragraph 13 cannot substitute for the product circular's paragraph 13.",
    "Paragraphs 15 and 16 have separate request conditions. Neither third-party verification nor a legal opinion becomes automatically required merely because the proposed footnote 5 minimum demonstration is activated.",
    "The supplied structural and retrieval checks establish neither legal support for the independent trigger nor substantive fulfillment."
  ],
